WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.334 --> 00:00:03.536
-So many of President Trump's
friends and aides

00:00:03.536 --> 00:00:06.172
have abandoned him that the
only people left to defend him

00:00:06.172 --> 00:00:08.141
are Stephen Miller
and Rudy Giuliani.

00:00:08.141 --> 00:00:10.743
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:10.743 --> 00:00:13.913
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:13.913 --> 00:00:17.049
Things would be
a lot easier for Trump

00:00:17.049 --> 00:00:19.719
if he still had Republicans
in Congress to protect him.

00:00:19.719 --> 00:00:22.054
But now he has to
deal with Democrats

00:00:22.054 --> 00:00:23.990
as they prepare to take control
of the House.

00:00:23.990 --> 00:00:26.392
And right now Trump is fighting
with them over the budget.

00:00:26.392 --> 00:00:27.793
Trump wants money
for his border wall,

00:00:27.793 --> 00:00:30.062
and Nancy Pelosi has been
adamant that he won't get it.

00:00:30.062 --> 00:00:32.165
And I'm just gonna guess,
from looking at the two of them,

00:00:32.165 --> 00:00:35.101
that Pelosi is going to win.

00:00:35.101 --> 00:00:37.002
I mean, look at the two of them.

00:00:37.002 --> 00:00:40.106
He looks like he had a panic
attack in a steam room,

00:00:40.106 --> 00:00:43.942
and she looks like
Neo from "The Matrix"

00:00:43.942 --> 00:00:47.213
if he shopped at Talbots.

00:00:47.213 --> 00:00:51.450
She's Tom Cruise.
He's "Risky Business."

00:00:51.450 --> 00:00:53.786
In fact, Trump is so easy
to beat in these situations

00:00:53.786 --> 00:00:56.122
that in last week's tense
meeting in the Oval Office,

00:00:56.122 --> 00:00:58.224
Pelosi called the potential
government shutdown

00:00:58.224 --> 00:01:00.192
a Trump shutdown,
and Trump was annoyed

00:01:00.192 --> 00:01:01.927
that Pelosi
beat him to the punch.

00:01:01.927 --> 00:01:04.163
-I think the
American people recognize

00:01:04.163 --> 00:01:06.632
that we must keep
government open,

00:01:06.632 --> 00:01:09.269
that a shutdown
is not worth anything

00:01:09.269 --> 00:01:11.871
and that you should not have
a Trump shutdown.

00:01:11.871 --> 00:01:14.974
-Oh, wait a minute.
Did you say Trump --

00:01:14.974 --> 00:01:16.376
Oh. That's what
I'm gonna call it.

00:01:16.376 --> 00:01:18.210
-You have your White House.
You have the Senate.

00:01:18.210 --> 00:01:20.079
-Oh, were you?

00:01:20.079 --> 00:01:22.548
Trump's like a guy
who gets checkmated in chess

00:01:22.548 --> 00:01:24.049
and says,
"I was gonna say that."

00:01:24.049 --> 00:01:25.918
And then you'd say,
"Why would you say that?

00:01:25.918 --> 00:01:27.286
You didn't checkmate me."

00:01:27.286 --> 00:01:30.756
Then he'd just eat
all the pieces.

00:01:30.756 --> 00:01:33.293
After Pelosi outwitted Trump
in the Oval Office meeting,

00:01:33.293 --> 00:01:35.027
the White House
got really desperate

00:01:35.027 --> 00:01:37.129
and turned to a staffer
who has mostly stayed

00:01:37.129 --> 00:01:38.464
out of the public eye lately,

00:01:38.464 --> 00:01:41.000
and that's senior policy advisor
Stephen Miller.

00:01:41.000 --> 00:01:44.637
[ Thunder crashes ]

00:01:44.637 --> 00:01:47.407
Miller has been quiet
in the last few weeks,

00:01:47.407 --> 00:01:50.944
although he occasionally lurks
in the backgrounds of photos

00:01:50.944 --> 00:01:56.649
like the White House janitor
who's been dead for 30 years.

00:01:56.649 --> 00:01:58.818
Yesterday, he went on
"Face the Nation"

00:01:58.818 --> 00:02:00.019
to aggressively proclaim

00:02:00.019 --> 00:02:01.954
that Trump would hold
the government hostage

00:02:01.954 --> 00:02:03.956
if he doesn't get money
for his border wall.

00:02:03.956 --> 00:02:06.726
-We are about five days from a
potential government shutdown,

00:02:06.726 --> 00:02:09.228
and Republican leadership says
there's no plan.

00:02:09.228 --> 00:02:12.097
What is the President's plan,
and will he shut it down

00:02:12.097 --> 00:02:14.066
to get this $5 billion
in border-wall funding?

00:02:14.066 --> 00:02:16.435
-We're going to do
whatever is necessary

00:02:16.435 --> 00:02:19.405
to build the border wall,
to stop this ongoing crisis

00:02:19.405 --> 00:02:20.874
of illegal immigration.

00:02:20.874 --> 00:02:22.174
-And that means a shutdown?

00:02:22.174 --> 00:02:23.476
-If it comes to it, absolutely.

00:02:23.476 --> 00:02:25.311
This is a very fundamental
issue.

00:02:25.311 --> 00:02:27.747
The Democrat Party
has a simple choice.

00:02:27.747 --> 00:02:30.349
They can either choose to fight
for America's working class

00:02:30.349 --> 00:02:32.251
or to promote
illegal immigration.

00:02:32.251 --> 00:02:33.920
You can't do both.

00:02:33.920 --> 00:02:35.855
-Yeah, uh-huh. Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:02:35.855 --> 00:02:38.624
Uh, what the hell's going on
with Stephen Miller's hair?

00:02:38.624 --> 00:02:43.328
I mean, here he is
before that interview.

00:02:43.328 --> 00:02:46.399
And here he is during it.

00:02:46.399 --> 00:02:50.803
Is that a proceeding hairline?

00:02:50.803 --> 00:02:53.839
Does Stephen Miller
get a hair hard-on

00:02:53.839 --> 00:02:56.342
when he talks about the wall?

00:02:56.342 --> 00:02:58.845
"Stephen, did you hear ICE
is breaking arrest records?"

00:02:58.845 --> 00:03:01.981
"Eww!

00:03:01.981 --> 00:03:06.519
Stephen has a hair boner!"

00:03:06.519 --> 00:03:07.753
I mean, look at that thing.

00:03:07.753 --> 00:03:09.388
It would have been
more believable

00:03:09.388 --> 00:03:12.191
if he just Charlie Brown'd it.

00:03:12.191 --> 00:03:15.194
Is that spray paint, or did he
get the inauguration crowd

00:03:15.194 --> 00:03:18.131
tattooed on his head?

00:03:18.131 --> 00:03:19.966
Trump was forced
to turn to Miller

00:03:19.966 --> 00:03:22.501
because of the unprecedented
turnover in his administration.

00:03:22.501 --> 00:03:24.237
For example, after
he announced the departure

00:03:24.237 --> 00:03:25.904
of his current chief of staff,
John Kelly,

00:03:25.904 --> 00:03:27.673
Trump said he would replace
Kelly with someone

00:03:27.673 --> 00:03:30.175
who already works in the
White House, Mick Mulvaney.

00:03:30.175 --> 00:03:32.512
And the White House said that
on top of being chief of staff,

00:03:32.512 --> 00:03:34.413
Mulvaney would also keep
his current job

00:03:34.413 --> 00:03:36.882
as the Director of the Office
of Management and Budget

00:03:36.882 --> 00:03:39.117
and the head of the Consumer
Financial Protection Bureau.

00:03:39.117 --> 00:03:41.320
It's getting to the point
where there's only going to be

00:03:41.320 --> 00:03:43.155
like four people left
in this administration

00:03:43.155 --> 00:03:45.491
and they're each
going to have 30 jobs.

00:03:45.491 --> 00:03:47.327
-"I'm pleased to announce that
I've appointed Stephen Miller

00:03:47.327 --> 00:03:50.229
Secretary of State, Defense,
Commerce, head speech writer,

00:03:50.229 --> 00:03:53.433
Communications Director,
and White House Babadook.

00:03:53.433 --> 00:03:55.535
[ Laughter ]

00:03:55.535 --> 00:03:59.738
And I have to say...
I have to say...

00:03:59.738 --> 00:04:02.208
Stephen is so excited about it,

00:04:02.208 --> 00:04:04.444
his hair boner
is down to his nose."

00:04:04.444 --> 00:04:06.912
[ Laughter ]

00:04:06.912 --> 00:04:08.681
Trump has lost Republicans
in Congress

00:04:08.681 --> 00:04:10.483
and Republicans
in his own White House,

00:04:10.483 --> 00:04:13.419
but, of course, the gravest
threat to his presidency so far

00:04:13.419 --> 00:04:15.588
came from the man who was,
for years, closer to him

00:04:15.588 --> 00:04:16.789
than almost anyone else,

00:04:16.789 --> 00:04:18.724
and that's his former lawyer,
Michael Cohen.

00:04:18.724 --> 00:04:20.492
In an interview with ABC,
Cohen made clear

00:04:20.492 --> 00:04:22.328
that Trump had directed him
to break the law

00:04:22.328 --> 00:04:25.063
and explained how he'd grown
apart from the President.

00:04:25.063 --> 00:04:26.899
-I will tell you
that the gentleman

00:04:26.899 --> 00:04:30.669
that is sitting now
in the Oval Office,

00:04:30.669 --> 00:04:32.771
1600 Pennsylvania Avenue,

00:04:32.771 --> 00:04:36.508
is not the Donald Trump that
I remember from Trump Tower.

00:04:36.508 --> 00:04:39.645
He's a very different
individual.

00:04:39.645 --> 00:04:42.281
-No, he's not
a different individual.

00:04:42.281 --> 00:04:45.318
He's just in
a different location.

00:04:45.318 --> 00:04:48.054
There's not an expression
"like a bull in a barn,"

00:04:48.054 --> 00:04:50.723
but move it to a china shop,
and suddenly everyone's like,

00:04:50.723 --> 00:04:52.524
"[Bleep].
Get this bull out of here!"

00:04:52.524 --> 00:04:54.460
They're like,
"He was fine in the barn."

00:04:54.460 --> 00:04:57.196
"This is not a [bleep] barn!"

00:04:57.196 --> 00:04:59.464
Now, Trump, for his part...

00:04:59.464 --> 00:05:01.200
for his part...

00:05:01.200 --> 00:05:03.402
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:03.402 --> 00:05:06.372
...has insisted that he had
nothing to do with the

00:05:06.372 --> 00:05:08.908
hush-money payments Cohen made
to cover up Trump's affairs.

00:05:08.908 --> 00:05:11.177
Trump has also argued that
Cohen should have known better,

00:05:11.177 --> 00:05:13.679
an argument he repeated
in an interview with Fox News.

00:05:13.679 --> 00:05:17.884
-Michael Cohen says that he lied
in order to protect you.

00:05:17.884 --> 00:05:19.485
-Yeah.
-What's your response to that?

00:05:19.485 --> 00:05:20.920
-Let me tell you.

00:05:20.920 --> 00:05:23.255
I never directed him
to do anything wrong.

00:05:23.255 --> 00:05:26.159
Whatever he did, he did
on his own. He's a lawyer.

00:05:26.159 --> 00:05:27.994
A lawyer who represents a client

00:05:27.994 --> 00:05:29.862
is supposed to do
the right thing.

00:05:29.862 --> 00:05:32.064
That's why you pay them a lot
of money, et cetera, et cetera.

00:05:32.064 --> 00:05:33.833
I think,
by "et cetera, et cetera,"

00:05:33.833 --> 00:05:36.168
you mean because it's illegal.

00:05:36.168 --> 00:05:38.904
Only Trump could
"et cetera, et cetera" the law.

00:05:38.904 --> 00:05:40.339
He pulled an Elaine.

00:05:40.339 --> 00:05:42.308
"I met a porn star,
went up to my room.

00:05:42.308 --> 00:05:46.212
Yada yada yada. I'm an
unindicted co-conspirator."

00:05:46.212 --> 00:05:47.746
Yet even in the last few days,

00:05:47.746 --> 00:05:49.248
Trump's story on this
has changed again.

00:05:49.248 --> 00:05:51.183
First, Trump insisted
he never heard of the payments.

00:05:51.183 --> 00:05:52.284
Then he said they were legal.

00:05:52.284 --> 00:05:53.686
Then he said
it was Cohen's fault.

00:05:53.686 --> 00:05:55.788
And now his current lawyer,
Rudy Giuliani, is saying...

00:05:55.788 --> 00:05:58.423
So what if it was illegal?
Nobody died.

00:05:58.423 --> 00:06:00.292
-Here's what Rudy Giuliani,
the President's lawyer,

00:06:00.292 --> 00:06:01.827
said this week.

00:06:01.827 --> 00:06:04.596
"Nobody got killed.
Nobody got robbed.

00:06:04.596 --> 00:06:08.267
This was not a big crime,"
Giuliani told The Daily Beast.

00:06:08.267 --> 00:06:10.136
And then he added,
"I think in two weeks

00:06:10.136 --> 00:06:13.706
they'll start with parking
tickets that haven't been paid."

00:06:13.706 --> 00:06:15.407
-This is ridiculous.

00:06:15.407 --> 00:06:17.042
And they're going around
with this,

00:06:17.042 --> 00:06:18.811
and you're talking about all
these other investigations.

00:06:18.811 --> 00:06:20.380
I'm telling you, George,
they're going to go try

00:06:20.380 --> 00:06:22.514
to look for
unpaid parking tickets.

00:06:22.514 --> 00:06:25.350
-Oh, my God. Rudy managed
to out-crazy Stephen Miller.

00:06:25.350 --> 00:06:29.088
Congrats, Rudy.
You get the hair boner.

00:06:29.088 --> 00:06:30.522
[ Laughter ]

00:06:30.522 --> 00:06:32.458
Even Trump's
closest friends and advisors

00:06:32.458 --> 00:06:34.894
are getting as far away from him
as they possibly can,

00:06:34.894 --> 00:06:36.962
and the only people
he has left to defend him

00:06:36.962 --> 00:06:38.497
are Rudy Giuliani
and Stephen Miller,

00:06:38.497 --> 00:06:40.465
and that's because people
are starting to realize

00:06:40.465 --> 00:06:42.869
a fundamental truth
about working for Donald Trump.

00:06:42.869 --> 00:06:46.405
You can keep your job or you
can keep your dignity, but...

00:06:46.405 --> 00:06:48.140
-You can't do both.

00:06:48.140 --> 00:06:50.743
-This has been "A Closer Look."

